@page "/"
@* V4 interpretation layer is frozen. No further conceptual changes allowed. *@

<PageTitle>TRM Cosmology</PageTitle>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h4" GutterBottom="true">Temporal Rate Matrix (TRM) Cosmology</MudText>

<MudCard Class="mb-3">
    <MudCardMedia Image="images/TRM-TQM-V3-Image1_Web_small.jpg" Height="200" alt="TRM space image" />
    <MudCardContent>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" GutterBottom="true"><b>Gravity from topology — not geometry</b></MudText>
        <MudStack Spacing="1">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
                Structural origin of the 1/r gravitational form from a discrete graph Laplacian — <b>DERIVED</b>.
            </MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
                GR-compatible weak-field behavior at 1PN (<LatexDisplay Content="$\beta_{\text{PPN}}\approx 1$" /> at <LatexDisplay Content="$b\approx 1.248$" />) — <b>SUPPORTED</b>.
            </MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
                UV-suppressed propagator <LatexDisplay Content="$D(k^2)\sim 1/k^6$" />, 1-loop finite — <b>VERIFIED</b> at 1-loop, conditional all-orders.
            </MudText>
        </MudStack>
    </MudCardContent>
</MudCard>

<MudPaper Class="pa-4 mb-3" Outlined="true">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" GutterBottom="true">How gravity emerges</MudText>
    <MudGrid Spacing="2">
        <MudItem xs="12" md="4">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Color="Color.Primary">Step 1 — Discrete Origin</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
                A network of coupled phase oscillators on a discrete lattice.
                Interactions are governed by a bilocal coupling matrix <LatexDisplay Content="$K_{ij}$" />.
            </MudText>
        </MudItem>
        <MudItem xs="12" md="4">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Color="Color.Primary">Step 2 — Emergence of Gravity</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
                A localized coupling defect in the graph Laplacian yields
                <LatexDisplay Content="$\nabla^2 K = 0$" />.
                The Green's function gives <LatexDisplay Content="$K(r)\sim 1/r$" /> — <b>DERIVED</b>.
            </MudText>
        </MudItem>
        <MudItem xs="12" md="4">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Color="Color.Primary">Step 3 — Physical Mapping</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
                <LatexDisplay Content="$\varphi(x) = \rho_E / \rho_{\text{ref}}$" /> — <b>HYPOTHESIS</b> (C5).
                Time-rate field <LatexDisplay Content="$T(x)$" /> yields acceleration
                <LatexDisplay Content="$a(x) = c^2 \nabla T(x)$" />.
                Newtonian limit reproduced — <b>SUPPORTED</b>.
            </MudText>
        </MudItem>
    </MudGrid>
</MudPaper>

<MudPaper Class="pa-4 mb-3" Outlined="true">
    <MudPaper Class="pa-3 mb-3" Outlined="true" Style="background: var(--mud-palette-info-hover, #F0F7FF);">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            <b>Structural contribution:</b> The 1/r gravitational form emerges from
            discrete graph Laplacian topology — <b>DERIVED</b>.
        </MudText>
    </MudPaper>
    <MudStack Spacing="1">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" GutterBottom="true">UV-scale behavior</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            A candidate UV-improved bilocal gravity framework
            with 1-loop verified finiteness and conditional all-orders convergence.
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            Kernel &rarr; Fourier transform:
            <LatexDisplay Content="$\mathcal{F}(k^2)\sim k^{-4}$" />
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            Propagator:
            <LatexDisplay Content="$D_{\text{TRM}}(k^2) = (1/k^2)\cdot\mathcal{F}(k^2) \sim 1/k^6$" />
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-2">
            Consequence: strong UV suppression &middot; 1-loop finite (<b>VERIFIED</b>) &middot;
            all-orders convergence (<b>CONDITIONAL</b> theorem, A1–A5).
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            GR propagator: <LatexDisplay Content="$D(k^2)\sim 1/k^2$" />
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-2">
            TRM propagator: <LatexDisplay Content="$D(k^2)\sim 1/k^6$" />
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="mb-2">
            UV modes are suppressed by the bilocal kernel form factor.
        </MudText>
        <img src="propagator_comparison.png" alt="GR (1/k²) vs TRM (1/k⁶) propagator scaling at high momentum" style="width:100%; max-width:560px; display:block;" />
        <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">
            At high momentum, the bilocal kernel form factor suppresses UV contributions as 1/k⁶, compared to the GR behavior 1/k².
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="mt-2">
            This stronger 1/k⁶ suppression implies that high-momentum (UV)
            contributions to loop integrals decay rapidly,
            leading to finite integrals.
            See <MudLink Href="/quantum-engine">Quantum Engine &amp; Loop Finiteness</MudLink> for the explicit computation.
        </MudText>
    </MudStack>
</MudPaper>

<MudPaper Class="pa-4 mb-3" Outlined="true">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" GutterBottom="true">Current verified features</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-2">
        At the current level of verification, the bilocal kernel framework supports the following properties:
    </MudText>
    <MudStack Spacing="1" Class="mb-2">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">&#8226; Ghost-free propagation (supported by spectral positivity and Padé kernel sign structure)</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">&#8226; 1-loop finiteness (explicitly verified; no counterterms required at 1-loop)</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">&#8226; Perturbative unitarity at 1-loop (<LatexDisplay Content="$\operatorname{Im}\Pi\geq 0,\;\rho\geq 0$" />)</MudText>
    </MudStack>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">
        These arise from the bilocal kernel structure.
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" GutterBottom="true" Class="mt-3">Why this matters</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-3">
        Quantum gravity faces a structural tradeoff: unitarity, finiteness, and ghost-freedom.
        GR is unitary and ghost-free but non-renormalizable; higher-derivative theories are
        finite but introduce ghosts. TRM resolves this via a bilocal form factor
        <LatexDisplay Content="$\mathcal{F}(k^2)\sim k^{-4}$" /> that suppresses UV modes without ghost degrees of freedom.
    </MudText>

    <MudTable Items="_comparisonRows" Dense="true" Hover="true" Bordered="true" Striped="true" Elevation="0">
        <HeaderContent>
            <MudTh>Approach</MudTh>
            <MudTh>Ghost-free</MudTh>
            <MudTh>Finite loops</MudTh>
            <MudTh>Unitary</MudTh>
        </HeaderContent>
        <RowTemplate>
            <MudTd>@context.Approach</MudTd>
            <MudTd>@context.GhostFree</MudTd>
            <MudTd>@context.FiniteLoops</MudTd>
            <MudTd>@context.Unitary</MudTd>
        </RowTemplate>
    </MudTable>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="mt-2">
        @TableFootnote
    </MudText>
</MudPaper>

<MudPaper Class="pa-4 mb-3" Outlined="true">
    <MudGrid Spacing="2">
        <MudItem xs="12" md="6">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Color="Color.Primary" GutterBottom="true">Framework Classification</MudText>
            <MudStack Spacing="1">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2"><b>FORM EXPLAINED</b> — the 1/r structure is <b>DERIVED</b> from network topology.</MudText>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2"><b>COEFFICIENT CALIBRATED</b> — <LatexDisplay Content="$G$" /> is <b>CALIBRATED</b> from observation.</MudText>
            </MudStack>
        </MudItem>
        <MudItem xs="12" md="6">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" GutterBottom="true">What TRM V4 does NOT claim</MudText>
            <MudStack Spacing="0">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">&#8226; Does <b>not</b> replace General Relativity</MudText>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">&#8226; Does <b>not</b> predict <LatexDisplay Content="$G$" /> from first principles</MudText>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">&#8226; Does <b>not</b> claim complete quantum gravity</MudText>
            </MudStack>
        </MudItem>
    </MudGrid>
</MudPaper>

<MudPaper Class="pa-4 mb-3" Outlined="true">
    <MudGrid Spacing="2">
        <MudItem xs="12" md="6">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" GutterBottom="true">Parameter Structure</MudText>
            <MudStack Spacing="0">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">&#8226; 1 free parameter: <LatexDisplay Content="$b$" /></MudText>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">&#8226; 2 empirical anchors: <LatexDisplay Content="$f_{\text{ref}}$" /> (cesium SI second), <LatexDisplay Content="$G$" /></MudText>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">&#8226; Comparable to GR (<LatexDisplay Content="$G, \Lambda$" />) or Brans-Dicke (<LatexDisplay Content="$\omega$" />)</MudText>
            </MudStack>
        </MudItem>
        <MudItem xs="12" md="6">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" GutterBottom="true">On the bilocal kernel</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
                The bilocal kernel is introduced as the minimal structure consistent with:
                Laplacian emergence of 1/r, Lorentzian stability, and UV suppression.
                It is <b>not</b> claimed as a fundamental microscopic derivation.
            </MudText>
        </MudItem>
    </MudGrid>
</MudPaper>

<MudPaper Class="pa-4 mb-3" Outlined="true">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" GutterBottom="true">How to read each dashboard</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">1) Set parameters in the left control panel.</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">2) Review the Physics Context box for formulas and current parameter values.</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">3) Compare chart/table outputs between GR reference and TRM prediction.</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="mt-2">
        See the <MudLink Href="/equations">Key Equations</MudLink> page for the full set of TRM formulas
        across all physical regimes.
    </MudText>
</MudPaper>

<MudPaper Class="pa-4 mt-3" Outlined="true">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Color="Color.Primary" GutterBottom="true">Conclusions</MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
        TRM provides a framework in which UV suppression, ghost-freedom, and perturbative
        unitarity are realized within a four-dimensional setting — consistent with the
        conditional all-orders convergence theorem (subject to assumptions A1–A5).
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mt-2">
        Cross-scale consistency with GR:
    </MudText>
    <MudStack Spacing="0" Class="ml-4">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">&#8226; Weak-field: <LatexDisplay Content="$\beta_{\text{PPN}},\gamma_{\text{PPN}}\to 1$" /> — solar-system tests recovered</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">&#8226; Strong-field: EFT analysis indicates GR-like behavior (<LatexDisplay Content="$\delta\ll 10^{-6}$" />) — <b>SUPPORTED</b></MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">&#8226; Scalar ODE: illustrative toy model only (<LatexDisplay Content="$r_H\approx 2.275\,GM$" />, +13.8%)</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">&#8226; Cosmological: <LatexDisplay Content="$g_{\text{TRM}}=g_N+\sqrt{g_N a_0}/\lambda$" /> — alternative to particle dark matter</MudText>
    </MudStack>
</MudPaper>

